Command Synatx for John the Ripper
  john --wordlist[path to wordlist] [Path to File]
    ex. john --wordlist=/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt hash_to_crack.txt
  john --format=[format] --wordlist[path to wordlist] [Path to File]
    ex. john --format=raw-md5 --wordlist=/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt hash_to_crack.txt
  john --list=formats | grep -iF "md5".   ##Best command to help find formatting
    NOTE: will pull md5 from the list of formats

  NOTE: Use raw-(format) to use basic format query

